{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>Benjamin.</b> He likened him to a wolf because he was mighty, and the sign is the men of Gibeah," "<b>ʿad.</b> Targum [of] spoil, and likewise \"then he divided the ʿad of spoil\" (Isaiah 33:23), \"for my day of rising up for ʿad\" (Zephaniah 3:8), \"a garment of ʿadim\" (Isaiah 64:5)." "<b>and at evening,</b> he divides the prey that he spoiled to his sons. And Yeshuʿa said: a hint to Saul, who defeated Amalek. And the meaning: in the morning, at the beginning of the kingdom; and at evening, in their exile on account of Mordecai — and this is the way of derash. And the opinion of the translator [Onkelos] in Aramaic is known."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:48:38.029221340Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}